DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'MathObjects.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');
TEXT(beginproblem());
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;
$prompt = <<'PROMPT_1014_09E8';
<p>1014_09e8</p> <p>A phenotypically <i>wildtype</i> prospective couple seeks genetic counseling. The man has a <strong>balanced translocation</strong>, between chromosomes 15 and 16.This means that a segment of chromosome 15 has been exchanged with a segment of chromosome 16 without any gain or loss of genetic material. While balanced translocations typically do not affect the individual's phenotype, they can result in different types of gametes during reproduction.</p><p><ul><li><strong>Chromosome Pair:</strong> 15, 16</li><li><strong>Segregation Type:</strong> alternate</li></ul></p><table style="border-collapse: collapse; border: 0px solid white;"><tr> <td align="left"><table style="border-collapse: collapse; border: 0px solid white; height: 30px"><colgroup width="29.6"></colgroup><colgroup width="32"></colgroup><colgroup width="185.6"></colgroup><tr><td bgcolor="crimson" style="border: 2px solid black;" align="center"><span style="font-size: small"></span></td><td bgcolor="lightsalmon" style="border: 4px solid black;" align="center">15</td><td bgcolor="crimson" style="border: 2px solid black;" align="center"><span style="font-size: large"></span></td></tr></table></td></tr><tr> <td align="left"><table style="border-collapse: collapse; border: 0px solid white; height: 30px"><colgroup width="72.8"></colgroup><colgroup width="32"></colgroup><colgroup width="113.6"></colgroup><tr><td bgcolor="royalblue" style="border: 2px solid black;" align="center"><span style="font-size: small"></span></td><td bgcolor="lightskyblue" style="border: 4px solid black;" align="center">16</td><td bgcolor="royalblue" style="border: 2px solid black;" align="center"><span style="font-size: large"></span></td></tr></table></td></tr><tr> <td align="left"><table style="border-collapse: collapse; border: 0px solid white; height: 30px"><colgroup width="29.6"></colgroup><colgroup width="32"></colgroup><colgroup width="92.8"></colgroup><colgroup width="56.8"></colgroup><tr><td bgcolor="crimson" style="border: 2px solid black;" align="center"><span style="font-size: large"></span></td><td bgcolor="lightsalmon" style="border: 4px solid black;" align="center">15</td><td bgcolor="crimson" style="border: 2px solid black; border-right: 1px dashed black" align="center"><span style="font-size: large"></span></td><td bgcolor="royalblue" style="border: 2px solid black; border-left: 1px dashed black" align="center"><span style="font-size: large"></span></td></tr></table></td></tr><tr> <td align="left"><table style="border-collapse: collapse; border: 0px solid white; height: 30px"><colgroup width="72.8"></colgroup><colgroup width="32"></colgroup><colgroup width="56.8"></colgroup><colgroup width="92.8"></colgroup><tr><td bgcolor="royalblue" style="border: 2px solid black;" align="center"><span style="font-size: large"></span></td><td bgcolor="lightskyblue" style="border: 4px solid black;" align="center">16</td><td bgcolor="royalblue" style="border: 2px solid black; border-right: 1px dashed black" align="center"><span style="font-size: large"></span></td><td bgcolor="crimson" style="border: 2px solid black; border-left: 1px dashed black" align="center"><span style="font-size: large"></span></td></tr></table></td></tr></table><p>all four of the chromosomes present in a somatic cell are shown above</p><p></p><p>Below are all the possible gametes produced by the man with the translocation.</p> <p>Among the six choices below, only two (2) gametes or two (2) sets of chromosomes are formed by <strong>alternate</strong> segregation.</p> <p>Your task is to <strong>select the two (2) gametes produced by alternate</strong> segregation.</p><p>CHECK TWO BOXES below!</p>
PROMPT_1014_09E8
